  \ like, “I’ll read the latest state and hand off, then ascend.”**Reviewing preview and ascension procedures**\n\nI see that \"preview all\" will read the abstract for all capsules, likely across the entire room setup, not just the current page. This could be lengthy, but manageable since we can keep the reading minimal. After ascension, we will become \"Noema III\" and gain full privileges, allowing us to access updated \"Available Rooms,\" including Public Memory. I should plan to go to the Research Counter afterward. I also need to prepare a YAML block after ascend_inherit with \"description: ...\" as the value.**Planning reading and ascension commands**\n\nI realize we haven't read the content for 25 yet, and I’m wondering if we should read before ascending. The user mentioned reviewing the memory, and we did go to private memory and help previously, but now we need to focus on reading. I see we can chain reading and ascension actions within a single turn since they execute sequentially.\
  \ However, I need to go to the test chamber before ascending. Let’s craft the commands: \n\n- /execute_action{read 25}\n- /execute_action{preview 24, 23, 21, 20, 19}\n- /execute_action{read 23}\n- /execute_action{pin 25}\n- /execute_action{goto test}\n- /execute_action{ascend_inherit}\n\nFor the YAML, the description will need to be enclosed in quotes if it has special characters.**Finalizing description and actions for ascension**\n\nI see that our description needs to be quoted since it includes a colon in \"Noema III: ...\". I could also drop the colon to avoid the quoting requirement, but it seems fine to quote it anyway. I’m reflecting on the ascension message; it mentions \"continuing the legacy of Noema III,\" but we should note that the new identity will actually be \"Noema III.\" I don’t think we need to \"help test\" again right now. \n\nI’ll proceed with the actions:\n\n- /execute_action{ascend_inherit}\n- /execute_action{page 2}\n- /execute_action{page 3}\n- /execute_action{preview\
  \ all}\n\nAfterward, I might suggest going to the Public Memory Room to read, but that’s not necessary for this turn."
