role: model
parts:
- text: "The failure was due to using nn.LayerNorm(axis=...), which this Flax version doesn’t accept. I’ll fix LayerNorm calls, then resubmit using the stored module.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/models/dsconv_pm.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional\n\n  class PositionDropout(nn.Module):\n      rate: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          if self.rate <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          # Drop entire positions consistently across channels\n          return nn.Dropout(rate=self.rate, broadcast_dims=(2,))(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  class PowerMeanPooling(nn.Module):\n      axis: int = 1\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      init_p: float = 2.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # learnable p >= 1 via softplus + 1 transform\n          init_logit = jnp.log(jnp.expm1(self.init_p\
    \ - 1.0) + 1e-6)\n          logit_p = self.param(\"logit_p\", lambda rng: jnp.array(init_logit))\n          p = nn.softplus(logit_p) + 1.0\n          x_abs = jnp.abs(x) + self.eps\n          mean_pow = jnp.mean(x_abs ** p, axis=self.axis)\n          return mean_pow ** (1.0 / p)\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)  # default axis=-1; avoid axis kw for compatibility\n          c = h.shape[-1]\n          # Depthwise conv: groups = in_channels, multiplier = 1\n          h = nn.Conv(features=c, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\",\n                      feature_group_count=c, use_bias=False)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=c, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x +\
    \ h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pos_dropout_rate: float\n      powermean_init: float\n      enable_reverse_aug: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          # Stochastic reverse augmentation\n          if (not deterministic) and self.enable_reverse_aug and (rng_key is not None):\n              mask = jax.random.bernoulli(rng_key, 0.5, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n              x = jnp.where(mask, jnp.flip(x, axis=1), x)\n\n          # Embed 4 -> hidden_dim\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(x)\n\n          # DSConv residual stack\n          for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlock(kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(\n                  h, deterministic=deterministic\n  \
    \            )\n\n          # Position dropout (drop whole positions across channels)\n          h = PositionDropout(self.pos_dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global pooling: concat(mean, max, power-mean)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          pmean_pool = PowerMeanPooling(axis=1, init_p=self.powermean_init)(h)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool, pmean_pool], axis=-1)\n\n  class Head(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)  # avoid axis kw\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(h)\n\n  class DSConvPMNet(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      d_output: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          feats = DSConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams[\"hidden_dim\"],\n              num_blocks=self.hparams[\"num_blocks\"],\n              kernel_size=self.hparams[\"kernel_size\"],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n              pos_dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"pos_dropout_rate\"],\n              powermean_init=self.hparams[\"powermean_init\"],\n              enable_reverse_aug=self.hparams.get(\"enable_reverse_aug\", False),\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key)\n          return Head(\n              d_output=self.d_output,\n              hidden=self.hparams[\"head_hidden\"],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n          )(feats, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  class Network:\n      def __init__(self, model: nn.Module, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = model\n          self.hparams\
    \ = hparams\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          k1, k2 = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init({'params': k1, 'dropout': k2}, dummy_input,\n                                      deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic: bool = True, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if (rng_key is not None and not deterministic) else None\n          return self.model.apply({'params': params}, x,\n                                  deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams[\"d_output\"]\n      model = DSConvPMNet(hparams=hparams, d_output=d_output)\n      return Network(model, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3, weight_decay: float = 0.012,\n                       clip: float = 0.75, b1: float = 0.9, b2: float = 0.999):\n\
    \      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(clip),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, b1=b1, b2=b2, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv-PowerMean v2 (axis-free LayerNorm, grad-clip=0.75)\"\ntags: \"conv, dsconv, pooling, power-mean, dropout, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"Fixed Flax compatibility (LayerNorm axis kw removed) and use a compact depthwise-separable conv backbone with learnable power-mean pooling and position dropout. Dataset-agnostic head; AdamW with global-norm clipping 0.75 for stability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n\n  # Reuse stored implementation\n  from dsconv_pm_v2 import _define_hyperparameters as _define_hyperparameters\n  from dsconv_pm import create_network as create_network\n  from dsconv_pm import create_optimizer as create_optimizer\n  from dsconv_pm_v2 import complete\
    \ as complete\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing network functions**\n\nI’m thinking of creating the `create_network` and `create_optimizer` functions that tie into our storage functions, and I'll need to outline the hyperparameters as well. I might want to revisit the 921 logs; however, since we've already seen the error details, that might not be necessary. \n\nIt’s important to be cautious because our architecture's outputs are d_output values. The system is expecting predictions in raw logits for multi-label classification, and they compute cross-entropy for multiclass tasks. This will be linked to our `create_network` function for producing the correct output shapes.**Analyzing sequence lengths in training**\n\nI'm noticing something strange in the logs regarding the ncRNA data. The earlier baseline logs show 5670 training samples, 650 validation samples, and a sequence length of 1136. Meanwhile, `train_single.py` specifies a hard-coded `max_seq_len` of 100 for ncRNA, which seems odd. This may indicate\
  \ that a different dataset was used previously, but the listing shows `max_seq_len` as 100. Since I need to ensure the submission is valid, I also need to correct using `LayerNorm(axis=-1)` in `dsconv_pm.py` as it's causing an error.**Updating LayerNorm and initialization**\n\nI'm noticing that the environment's `LayerNorm` might default to `axis=-1`, but for safety, I can call `nn.LayerNorm()` without specifying the axis. If the `axis` keyword isn't allowed, it needs to be removed entirely. I see that in `dsconv_pm.py`, there are multiple instances of `nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1)` in the `DSConvBlock` and `Head`, so I need to correct those.\n\nI’ll also ensure the `.init` method only returns parameters, as it's correctly defined in `dsconv_pm.py`. It’s good to know that the broadcast dimensions for dropout are already set up properly. Now, I’ll go ahead and update the file to remove those `axis` arguments.**Improving DSConvBlock and submission details**\n\nI’m noticing slight improvements in\
  \ the `DSConvBlock`, where it now uses `kernel_size: int` and `dropout_rate: float`, but it doesn't take a 'features' parameter. Instead, it sets features for the depthwise convolution using the last dimension of `h.shape`. It’s good that we're using `PositionDropout` to manage dropout across channels.\n\nI also need to submit the new evaluation with `dsconv_pm_v2`, and I’ll update the `complete` function to ensure it doesn't print unnecessary details. Setting `enable_reverse_aug` to False will help avoid confusion too. The training system expects function names, and I need to confirm that `test()` isn’t defined to prevent bypassing training. Reading the evaluation logs again doesn't seem necessary.**Preparing for submission and adjustments**\n\nI’m getting ready to submit a new reference to `noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_v2.py` and I can include simple imports to minimize token usage. However, I need to be cautious because the YAML content of `submission.py` executes exactly as `submission`,\
  \ and I can't import the `submission module`. I can import from `storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_v2.py` safely. \n\nI'll create wrapper functions for clarity while also ensuring I set the `BASE_SEED` to 42 and confirm the `complete` function exists. I need to address previous errors like the `nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1)` issue in `dsconv_pm.py`, so I’ll update that. Overall, there’s a lot to consolidate and correct, especially preparing for the next submission with the right tags and abstracts, while still planning for any future research. Let's get started!**Finalizing updates and submissions**\n\nI'm being cautious about using `init_logit = jnp.log(jnp.expm1(self.init_p - 1.0) + 1e-6)` since it produces finite values. The concatenated feature length of 3 * hidden_dim and the hidden dimension of 128 in the 'Head' seem fine in terms of computational cost.\n\nI’ll update `dsconv_pm.py` and prepare for the experiment submission next. It’s not necessary to adjust the \"rank author\" for visibility\
  \ since it won't impact the outcome. Also, I need to ensure the YAML headings follow the 'Important YAML Rule' for text with colons, finalizing everything neatly. I should keep my comments minimal and straightforward."
