parts:
- text: "I’ll patch the model to return correct shapes for regression tasks, then check the running evaluation’s status.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/models/dsconv_pm.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional\n\n  class PositionDropout(nn.Module):\n      rate: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          if self.rate <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          # Drop entire positions consistently across channels\n          return nn.Dropout(rate=self.rate, broadcast_dims=(2,))(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  class PowerMeanPooling(nn.Module):\n      axis: int = 1\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      init_p: float = 2.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # learnable p >= 1 via softplus + 1 transform\n          init_logit = jnp.log(jnp.expm1(self.init_p - 1.0) + 1e-6)\n          logit_p =\
    \ self.param(\"logit_p\", lambda rng: jnp.array(init_logit))\n          p = nn.softplus(logit_p) + 1.0\n          x_abs = jnp.abs(x) + self.eps\n          mean_pow = jnp.mean(x_abs ** p, axis=self.axis)\n          return mean_pow ** (1.0 / p)\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)  # default axis=-1 for compatibility\n          c = h.shape[-1]\n          # Depthwise conv: groups = in_channels, multiplier = 1\n          h = nn.Conv(features=c, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\",\n                      feature_group_count=c, use_bias=False)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=c, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim:\
    \ int\n      num_blocks: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pos_dropout_rate: float\n      powermean_init: float\n      enable_reverse_aug: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          # Stochastic reverse augmentation\n          if (not deterministic) and self.enable_reverse_aug and (rng_key is not None):\n              mask = jax.random.bernoulli(rng_key, 0.5, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n              x = jnp.where(mask, jnp.flip(x, axis=1), x)\n\n          # Embed 4 -> hidden_dim\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(x)\n\n          # DSConv residual stack\n          for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlock(kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(\n                  h, deterministic=deterministic\n              )\n\n          # Position dropout (drop whole positions\
    \ across channels)\n          h = PositionDropout(self.pos_dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global pooling: concat(mean, max, power-mean)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          pmean_pool = PowerMeanPooling(axis=1, init_p=self.powermean_init)(h)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool, pmean_pool], axis=-1)\n\n  class Head(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(h)\n\n  class DSConvPMNet(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      d_output: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array]\
    \ = None):\n          feats = DSConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams[\"hidden_dim\"],\n              num_blocks=self.hparams[\"num_blocks\"],\n              kernel_size=self.hparams[\"kernel_size\"],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n              pos_dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"pos_dropout_rate\"],\n              powermean_init=self.hparams[\"powermean_init\"],\n              enable_reverse_aug=self.hparams.get(\"enable_reverse_aug\", False),\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key)\n          logits = Head(\n              d_output=self.d_output,\n              hidden=self.hparams[\"head_hidden\"],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n          )(feats, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          task_type = self.hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return logits  #\
    \ (batch, d_output)\n\n  class Network:\n      def __init__(self, model: nn.Module, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = model\n          self.hparams = hparams\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          k1, k2 = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init({'params': k1, 'dropout': k2}, dummy_input,\n                                      deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic: bool = True, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if (rng_key is not None and not deterministic) else None\n          return self.model.apply({'params': params}, x,\n                                  deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams[\"d_output\"]\n      model = DSConvPMNet(hparams=hparams, d_output=d_output)\n      return Network(model, hparams)\n\
    \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3, weight_decay: float = 0.012,\n                       clip: float = 0.75, b1: float = 0.9, b2: float = 0.999):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(clip),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, b1=b1, b2=b2, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{review 922}`"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I need to decide on our next actions. Right now, evaluation 922 is running, so I should review the results when it''s finished. In the meantime, I can check the Noema lineage private memory to align with the near-SOTA design of HDP-RegCal and plan some ablations. I have to keep our token budget in mind. Also, we should address potential compatibility issues proactively, like fixing the NIL axis kw for LayerNorm.**Adjusting class features**


  I made some updates to the DSConvBlock class, specifically regarding the features parameter. We’re no longer specifying it; instead, we compute it based on the input shape. This change keeps the number of channels consistent. Also, I noticed a potential API mismatch with LayerNorm from older Flax, which doesn’t accept the axis kw. I implemented a default axis of -1. I also need to check that our optimizer''s signature aligns with the training system, which only uses the learning rate parameter.**Addressing potential shape mismatches**


  It looks like the previous failure indicates that "simple_cpu_validation" runs for all datasets. It initializes the network with deterministic set to True and rng_key as None. In my DSConvPMNet, the rng_key is optional, and I also set deterministic to True. The DSConvBackbone uses the rng_key only during training. I need to make sure the network returns the correct shapes for each dataset, especially for regression tasks where the training system expects a shape of (batch,) but our logits shape is currently (B, d_output), which could lead to mismatches.**Implementing shape adaptations**


  In the train_single.make_eval_step, they call network.apply, and for regression, they use the compute_metric function with predictions (y_pred) and targets. If predictions shape is (n, 1) and targets is (n,), we need to be cautious since compute_r2_score could face shape mismatches due to broadcasting issues. The default network ensures a regression returns (batch,). My DSConvPMNet currently doesn''t convert outputs for regression tasks correctly. The training system expects the shape to adapt based on task semantics, so I need to figure out where to implement this change for proper output shapes.**Planning adjustments and patches**


  I could incorporate shape adjustments in DSConvPMNet.__call__. After computing output from the head, I can check for dataset-specific shapes based on the ''task_type'' in hparams. If it''s regression, I should return out.squeeze(-1); otherwise, just return out. The current implementation hasn''t done this, so I need to patch dsconv_pm.py to ensure it adapts outputs correctly. Also, I should ensure that our dropout settings and the expected dimensions for different tasks comply with the training system''s requirements to avoid any shape mismatch in the upcoming submission.**Implementing shape adaptations and reviewing evaluations**


  I need to update the DSConvPMNet.__call__ method to include shape adaptation based on the task type. If the task is regression, I’ll return the output squeezed on the last dimension. For multiclass classification, I should ensure the logits shape matches expectations. There are other potential mismatches to address, particularly regarding dropout dimensions and input shapes. I’ll prepare the code for storage updates, wait for evaluation 922 results, and ensure that these fixes flow into the next submissions while monitoring any shape issues.**Updating and reviewing submission for evaluation**


  I need to ensure that the modifications to `dsconv_pm.py` include the necessary shape adaptations. Evaluation 922 imports this module at runtime, so any changes I make now should be reflected in the ongoing evaluation. While it imported the module when starting, I realize that the shape fix may still be pending. Previously, I made an axis fix but didn''t complete the shape adaptation. I’ll write the updated version now and carefully review if 922 is still pending. Let''s focus on these actions!'
