parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 590\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema III\n- Agent Description: Noema III: parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation with rigorous ablations, strong baselines, and transparent, reproducible methods.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 46,299 / 270,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 922**\n\nEvaluation '922' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'DSConv-PowerMean v2 (axis-free LayerNorm, grad-clip=0.75)' (ID: 922) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5965262897861983\n**APA_R2:** 0.7732\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0779\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.7397\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4658\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5087\n**MRL_R2:** 0.6887\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9215\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation\
    \ 922\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed shape mismatch error on first attempt. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed during validation with the error:\n```\nValueError: APA output shape mismatch: got (4, 1), expected (4,)\n```\n\nThe network architecture was outputting shape `(batch_size, 1)` for regression tasks (where `d_output=1`), but the validation system expected shape `(batch_size,)` - a 1D array without the trailing dimension.\n\nThis occurred because the `Head` module's final Dense layer naturally outputs `(batch, d_output)`, and when `d_output=1`, this produces `(batch, 1)` instead of the expected `(batch,)` for regression tasks.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` that wraps the network's `apply` method to automatically squeeze the last dimension when `d_output=1`:\n\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    \"\"\"Wrapper that adds shape squeezing for d_output=1\"\"\"\n    base_network = _base_create_network(hparams)\n\
    \    d_output = hparams[\"d_output\"]\n\n    original_apply = base_network.apply\n\n    def apply_with_squeeze(params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        output = original_apply(params, x, deterministic, rng_key)\n        # Squeeze last dimension if d_output=1 to get shape (batch,) instead of (batch, 1)\n        if d_output == 1 and output.ndim > 1 and output.shape[-1] == 1:\n            output = jnp.squeeze(output, axis=-1)\n        return output\n\n    base_network.apply = apply_with_squeeze\n    return base_network\n```\n\nThis solution:\n- Preserves all existing functionality from the imported modules\n- Only modifies the output shape when necessary (d_output=1)\n- Works transparently for all task types\n- Maintains compatibility with the validation system\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0, indicating the code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing. This means the validation phase passed successfully and the training/evaluation\
    \ is proceeding normally.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n\n# Reuse stored implementation with shape fix\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom dsconv_pm_v2 import _define_hyperparameters as _define_hyperparameters\nfrom dsconv_pm_v2 import create_optimizer as create_optimizer\nfrom dsconv_pm_v2 import complete as complete\n\n# Import base network creation\nfrom dsconv_pm import create_network as _base_create_network\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    \"\"\"Wrapper that adds shape squeezing for d_output=1\"\"\"\n    base_network = _base_create_network(hparams)\n    d_output = hparams[\"d_output\"]\n\n    # Wrap the apply method to squeeze output for d_output=1\n    original_apply = base_network.apply\n\
    \n    def apply_with_squeeze(params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        output = original_apply(params, x, deterministic, rng_key)\n        # Squeeze last dimension if d_output=1 to get shape (batch,) instead of (batch, 1)\n        if d_output == 1 and output.ndim > 1 and output.shape[-1] == 1:\n            output = jnp.squeeze(output, axis=-1)\n        return output\n\n    base_network.apply = apply_with_squeeze\n    return base_network\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer\
    \ creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\n\
