parts:
- text: "922 establishes a solid DSConv baseline (0.5965). To isolate contributions from our new components, I’ll:\n- Check 924’s status\n- Prepare ablation wrappers\n- Run one ablation (disable eval-time bi-reverse; keep train reverse) to measure its effect\n\n`/execute_action{review 924}`\n`/execute_action{rank author}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_ablate_eval_only.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n  from dsconv_pm import create_network as create_network\n  from dsconv_pm import create_optimizer as _opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Match v3 except turn OFF eval-time bi-reverse averaging.\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 1e-3,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 224,\n          \"num_blocks\": 6,\n          \"kernel_size\": 9,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"pos_dropout_rate\": 0.07,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"powermean_init\"\
    : 2.0,\n          \"enable_reverse_aug\": True,   # keep training-time reverse augmentation\n          \"eval_bireverse\": False,      # ablation: disable eval-time averaging\n          \"residual_scale\": 0.5,\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3):\n      return _opt(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012, clip=0.75, b1=0.85, b2=0.99)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get(\"dataset\")\n      val = trial_data.get(\"val_metric\")\n      seed = trial_data.get(\"seed\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] (Abl-EvalOnly) {ds} val_metric={val} seed={seed}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_ablate_train_only.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n  from dsconv_pm import create_network as create_network\n  from dsconv_pm import create_optimizer as _opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Match v3 except\
    \ turn OFF training-time reverse augmentation.\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 1e-3,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 224,\n          \"num_blocks\": 6,\n          \"kernel_size\": 9,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"pos_dropout_rate\": 0.07,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"powermean_init\": 2.0,\n          \"enable_reverse_aug\": False,  # ablation: disable training-time augmentation\n          \"eval_bireverse\": True,       # keep eval-time averaging\n          \"residual_scale\": 0.5,\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3):\n      return _opt(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012, clip=0.75, b1=0.85, b2=0.99)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get(\"dataset\")\n      val = trial_data.get(\"val_metric\")\n      seed = trial_data.get(\"seed\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] (Abl-TrainOnly) {ds} val_metric={val} seed={seed}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_ablate_residual1.py}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n  from dsconv_pm import create_network as create_network\n  from dsconv_pm import create_optimizer as _opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Match v3 except set residual_scale back to 1.0\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 1e-3,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 224,\n          \"num_blocks\": 6,\n          \"kernel_size\": 9,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"pos_dropout_rate\": 0.07,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"powermean_init\": 2.0,\n          \"enable_reverse_aug\": True,\n          \"eval_bireverse\": True,\n          \"residual_scale\": 1.0,  # ablation: no residual scaling\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3):\n      return _opt(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012, clip=0.75, b1=0.85, b2=0.99)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get(\"dataset\"\
    )\n      val = trial_data.get(\"val_metric\")\n      seed = trial_data.get(\"seed\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] (Abl-Residual1) {ds} val_metric={val} seed={seed}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: DSConv-PM v3 without eval-time bi-reverse averaging\"\ntags: \"conv, dsconv, pooling, augmentation, ablation, optimizer-adamw\"\nabstract: \"Isolates the effect of eval-time bi-directional averaging by disabling it while keeping training-time reverse augmentation and all other hyperparameters identical to v3.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pm_ablate_eval_only import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer, complete\n  from dsconv_pm_ablate_eval_only import create_network as create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating evaluation strategies**


  I''m thinking that using eval-time bireverse could improve things, but I also need to test its contributions. The scoreboard ranking has evaluation-specific changes that might limit its effectiveness. I really want to focus on simplicity and insights, so I''ll design minimal adjustments and include method tags. I''ll also ensure we store the test code. Let’s prepare to submit ablation ''A'' without eval_bireverse. We might need to review responses next, and I''ll consider adding optional tests to wrappers if necessary.**Addressing shape and functionality**


  I''m noticing potential shape issues in our DSConvPMNet. It returns logits squeezed only for regression tasks, while multi-class classification for ''ncRNA'' expects a shape of (batch, 13) logits, which is fine! For the Modif, the shape is (batch, 12), so that looks good too. I''ll use dropout by passing the rng_key during training, specifically in training_single for dropout_key. Now, I''ll list final actions to execute, such as reviewing, storing ablation files, and submitting the eval-only fix.**Planning ablation submissions**


  I''m thinking we''ll write all three ablations, but I can only submit the first one right now. I should set up the commands: first to review and then potentially rank the author.


  Next, I''ll write the ablation code for submission. It''s crucial to import the wrapper''s functions and format the YAML correctly. I’ll use triple backticks for the content and ensure titles don’t include colons or Greek characters since we want to keep it simple. I’ll also make sure to limit the tags count to six. Finally, considering reading from Private Memory for baseline design might be useful, but it’s not essential.**Crafting action plan**


  I''m thinking about crafting the answer with clear actions and maybe adding a brief reflection note, though not a memory. Since the environment only processes commands and YAML, I want to keep extra text to a minimum.


  After I get the results, I''ll focus on calibrating Modif classification. I might incorporate label smoothing or adjust the threshold, but I can''t change the loss function. However, I can modify the architecture using gating and multi-kernel features while keeping it simple. I’ll wrap that up in the final steps!'
