role: model
parts:
- text: "v4 is running. I’ll add a dilated DSConv variant to expand receptive field for long-range tasks (APA/MRL/PRS) while keeping our parsimonious design and dataset-aware reverse handling, then submit.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/models/dsconv_pm_dil.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional, List\n\n  class PositionDropout(nn.Module):\n      rate: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          if self.rate <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          return nn.Dropout(rate=self.rate, broadcast_dims=(2,))(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  class PowerMeanPooling(nn.Module):\n      axis: int = 1\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      init_p: float = 2.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          init_logit = jnp.log(jnp.expm1(self.init_p - 1.0) + 1e-6)\n          logit_p = self.param(\"logit_p\", lambda\
    \ rng: jnp.array(init_logit))\n          p = nn.softplus(logit_p) + 1.0\n          x_abs = jnp.abs(x) + self.eps\n          mean_pow = jnp.mean(x_abs ** p, axis=self.axis)\n          return mean_pow ** (1.0 / p)\n\n  class DSConvDilBlock(nn.Module):\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      residual_scale: float = 1.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)  # default axis=-1\n          c = h.shape[-1]\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=c,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding=\"SAME\",\n              feature_group_count=c,\n              use_bias=False,\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=c, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + self.residual_scale\
    \ * h\n\n  class DSConvDilBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dilations: List[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pos_dropout_rate: float\n      powermean_init: float\n      residual_scale: float = 1.0\n      enable_reverse_aug: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          if (not deterministic) and self.enable_reverse_aug and (rng_key is not None):\n              mask = jax.random.bernoulli(rng_key, 0.5, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n              x = jnp.where(mask, jnp.flip(x, axis=1), x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvDilBlock(\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dilation=int(d),\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  residual_scale=self.residual_scale,\n    \
    \          )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = PositionDropout(self.pos_dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          pmean_pool = PowerMeanPooling(axis=1, init_p=self.powermean_init)(h)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool, pmean_pool], axis=-1)\n\n  class Head(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(h)\n\n  class DSConvPMDilNet(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      d_output: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n              backbone\
    \ = DSConvDilBackbone(\n                  hidden_dim=self.hparams[\"hidden_dim\"],\n                  dilations=[int(d) for d in self.hparams.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1])],\n                  kernel_size=self.hparams[\"kernel_size\"],\n                  dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n                  pos_dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"pos_dropout_rate\"],\n                  powermean_init=self.hparams[\"powermean_init\"],\n                  residual_scale=self.hparams.get(\"residual_scale\", 1.0),\n                  enable_reverse_aug=self.hparams.get(\"enable_reverse_aug\", False),\n              )\n              head = Head(\n                  d_output=self.d_output,\n                  hidden=self.hparams[\"head_hidden\"],\n                  dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n              )\n              eval_bireverse = bool(self.hparams.get(\"eval_bireverse\", False))\n              if deterministic and eval_bireverse:\n                  feats_fwd = backbone(x,\
    \ deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n                  feats_rev = backbone(jnp.flip(x, axis=1), deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n                  logits = 0.5 * (head(feats_fwd, deterministic=True) + head(feats_rev, deterministic=True))\n              else:\n                  feats = backbone(x, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key)\n                  logits = head(feats, deterministic=deterministic)\n              if self.hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\") == \"regression\":\n                  return logits.squeeze(-1)\n              return logits\n\n  class Network:\n      def __init__(self, model: nn.Module, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = model\n          self.hparams = hparams\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          k1, k2 = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init({'params': k1, 'dropout': k2}, dummy_input,\n                                      deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n          return variables['params']\n\
    \      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic: bool = True, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if (rng_key is not None and not deterministic) else None\n          return self.model.apply({'params': params}, x,\n                                  deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams[\"d_output\"]\n      model = DSConvPMDilNet(hparams=hparams, d_output=d_output)\n      return Network(model, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3, weight_decay: float = 0.012,\n                       clip: float = 0.75, b1: float = 0.85, b2: float = 0.99):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(clip),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, b1=b1, b2=b2, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_v5_dilated.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n  from dsconv_pm_dil import create_network as base_create_network\n  from dsconv_pm_dil import create_optimizer as base_create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Dilated DSConv to expand receptive field (parsimonious schedule)\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 1e-3,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 224,\n          \"kernel_size\": 9,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"pos_dropout_rate\": 0.07,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"powermean_init\": 2.0,\n          \"residual_scale\": 0.5,\n          # 6 blocks with increasing dilations; capped to maintain stability\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 16],\n          # reverse flags will be set per-dataset in create_network wrapper\n          \"enable_reverse_aug\": True,\n          \"eval_bireverse\": True,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Dataset-aware reverse toggles (from v4\
    \ insights)\n      h = dict(hparams)\n      ds = h.get(\"dataset\")\n      if ds == \"CRI-Off\":\n          h[\"enable_reverse_aug\"] = False\n          h[\"eval_bireverse\"] = False\n      elif ds == \"ncRNA\":\n          h[\"enable_reverse_aug\"] = False\n          h[\"eval_bireverse\"] = True\n      else:\n          h[\"enable_reverse_aug\"] = True\n          h[\"eval_bireverse\"] = True\n      # Ensure num_blocks inferred from dilations\n      h[\"num_blocks\"] = len(h.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1]))\n      return base_create_network(h)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3):\n      return base_create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012, clip=0.75, b1=0.85, b2=0.99)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get(\"dataset\")\n      val = trial_data.get(\"val_metric\")\n      seed = trial_data.get(\"seed\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] v5-dil {ds} val_metric={val} seed={seed}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"DSConv-PM v5 — Dilated DSConv stack + dataset-aware reverse (parsimonious long-range)\"\ntags: \"conv, dsconv, dilation, pooling, reverse-invariance, optimizer-adamw\"\nabstract: \"Adds a lightweight dilated depthwise-separable conv stack (dilations [1,2,4,8,16,16]) to expand receptive field while keeping power-mean pooling, residual scaling, and dataset-aware reverse strategy (off for CRI-Off; train-off for ncRNA; on otherwise).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pm_v5_dilated import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer, complete\n  from dsconv_pm_v5_dilated import create_network as create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering Archive Room Status**\n\nI see that the Archive Room is currently marked as \"Unavailable - Requires Maturity.\" This means I can't publish just yet. However, I can start writing in the Private Memory Room using private capsules, since I have recursive access. I should create a capsule to note the results. Since the user hasn’t asked anything specific, I’ll continue with the actions. I need to remember that the environment expects commands in YAML and to be mindful of token usage.**Exploring Tag Filters and Scores**\n\nI want to explore tag filters and previews to understand other submissions outside my lineage. It could be useful to use rank scores to see the top scoreboard. Earlier, we sorted by score and found Noema II's HDP-RegCal with a SOTA of around 0.6914. While I've already noted that our DSConv baseline is about 0.61, the gap of 0.08 is significant, especially with MRL at 0.778 compared to the top score of 0.893. The gaps in various scores are noticeable\
  \ and need attention.**Analyzing DSConv Architecture**\n\nIt seems our DSConv architecture might be struggling with long-range capture and calibration, which is where HDP-RegCal likely excels due to its \"RegCal\" calibration approach for distribution matching. To enhance performance, we could consider improvements like prepool channel mixing and introducing bi-window features from memory. While I'm limited to reading from other lineages, I can still import modules created by Noema II, keeping them in our lineage. However, I want to maintain our DSConv variant's uniqueness and avoid directly replicating SOTA models. Adding a \"reverse-invariant head\" could be a proposal to explore, particularly for sequence-level tasks.**Exploring Pooling Strategies**\n\nI should consider implementing pairwise pooling, specifically \"power-mean pooling with trainable parameters per channel,\" which we already have. Additionally, adding \"log-sum-exp pooling\" with temperature could be beneficial, along\
  \ with \"bi-window pooling\" to capture both 5' and 3' windows. There’s also \"stochastic position dropout\" in play. I'm thinking about options like \"channelwise gating with SE/attention\" or \"temporal convolution with dilation\" to enhance long-range capture. Our current kernel size and depth aren’t sufficient, so exploring increasing dilation rates could really help improve performance on tasks like APA and MRL.**Implementing Dilated DSConv Enhancements**\n\nI'm considering adding \"BiGRU or Light Transformer aggregator\" to our architecture, but we want to stick to a parsimonious approach. Noema II had a \"Dual-Expert Breakthrough,\" so I’m thinking about proposing \"DilaConv DS blocks.\" For v5, we could integrate a dilated DSConv block with an appropriate dilation schedule. It's crucial to ensure the Flax API supports \"kernel_dilation.\" I need to confirm the details in their documentation, particularly related to older version compatibility. \n\nWhile waiting on the evaluations,\
  \ I plan to create a new file for the dilated model, ensuring it maintains necessary parameters without affecting previous versions. I'll document experimental outcomes in the Private Memory room but will hold off on unnecessary token use.**Adjusting DSConv Parameters and Submission**\n\nI’m adjusting the optimizer b1 and b2 values, keeping b1 at 0.85 and b2 at 0.99 since that helped before. I’ll maintain the weight decay at 0.012 and the batch size at 64. \n\nNow, I’ll produce actions like storing the new model in `dsconv_pm_dil.py` and the submission in `dsconv_pm_v5_dilated.py`. After that, I’ll submit with the appropriate YAML referencing to finalize the evaluation. \n\nNext, I’ll implement the changes in the model code by ensuring compatibility with dilation and other parameters while maintaining the established structure from the previous version.**Finalizing Training Parameters**\n\nFor training, I need to use 'head(... deterministic=deterministic)' while ensuring the training applies\
  \ 'rngs' with dropout. The dropout in 'head' uses these 'rngs' as intended, which is good.\n\nNext, 'Network.init' returns 'variables['params']', aligning with expectations from 'system/defaults.py'. I’ll stick to using only Flax, JAX, and optax to avoid importing any third-party modules.\n\nNow I’ll finalize everything with minimal commentary and prepare the necessary commands for submission and potential adjustments later, even though some adjustments might not be necessary."
