role: model
parts:
- text: "v4 hurt ncRNA and PRS; ablations show both training reverse and eval bi-reverse should stay ON for all datasets. I’ll run a global-reverse dilated variant to target long-range tasks.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_v5_dilated_global.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n  from dsconv_pm_dil import create_network as base_create_network\n  from dsconv_pm_dil import create_optimizer as base_create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Dilated DSConv with global reverse augmentation and bi-reverse eval ON for all datasets\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 1e-3,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 224,\n          \"kernel_size\": 9,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"pos_dropout_rate\": 0.07,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"powermean_init\": 2.0,\n          \"residual_scale\": 0.5,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8,\
    \ 16, 16],\n          \"enable_reverse_aug\": True,\n          \"eval_bireverse\": True,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Pass through unchanged to keep reverse features ON everywhere\n      h = dict(hparams)\n      h[\"num_blocks\"] = len(h.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1]))\n      return base_create_network(h)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3):\n      return base_create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012, clip=0.75, b1=0.85, b2=0.99)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get(\"dataset\")\n      val = trial_data.get(\"val_metric\")\n      seed = trial_data.get(\"seed\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] v5g-dil {ds} val_metric={val} seed={seed}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv-PM v5g — Dilated DSConv + global reverse augmentation and bi-reverse eval\"\ntags: \"conv, dsconv, dilation, pooling, augmentation, optimizer-adamw\"\nabstract: \"Global variant of v5: dilated\
    \ depthwise-separable conv stack (dilations [1,2,4,8,16,16]) with power-mean pooling and residual scaling. Training-time reverse augmentation and eval-time bi-directional averaging are enabled for all datasets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pm_v5_dilated_global import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer, complete\n  from dsconv_pm_v5_dilated_global import create_network as create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
