tick: 597
role: model
parts:
- text: "v5 (dilated DSConv) substantially improved APA/MRL/Modif and overall score (0.6445), but ncRNA and CRI-On still lag. I’ll add a lightweight attention pooling head (task-type aware) atop the dilated backbone to boost classification (ncRNA) and small-data robustness (CRI-On), while keeping parsimony and global reverse augmentation.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/models/dsconv_pm_dil_attn.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional, List\n\n  class PositionDropout(nn.Module):\n      rate: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          if self.rate <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          return nn.Dropout(rate=self.rate, broadcast_dims=(2,))(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  class PowerMeanPooling(nn.Module):\n      axis: int = 1\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      init_p: float = 2.0\n      @nn.compact\n     \
    \ def __call__(self, x):\n          init_logit = jnp.log(jnp.expm1(self.init_p - 1.0) + 1e-6)\n          logit_p = self.param(\"logit_p\", lambda rng: jnp.array(init_logit))\n          p = nn.softplus(logit_p) + 1.0\n          x_abs = jnp.abs(x) + self.eps\n          mean_pow = jnp.mean(x_abs ** p, axis=self.axis)\n          return mean_pow ** (1.0 / p)\n\n  class AttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_hidden: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          # Simple content-based attention: a = softmax(W2 tanh(W1 x))\n          h = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_hidden)(x))           # (B, L, d_hidden)\n          a = nn.Dense(1)(h)                                # (B, L, 1)\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(a, axis=1)                     # (B, L, 1)\n          return jnp.sum(w * x, axis=1)                     # (B, C)\n\n  class DSConvDilBlock(nn.Module):\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n\
    \      residual_scale: float = 1.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)  # default axis=-1\n          c = h.shape[-1]\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=c,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding=\"SAME\",\n              feature_group_count=c,\n              use_bias=False,\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=c, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + self.residual_scale * h\n\n  class DSConvDilBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dilations: List[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pos_dropout_rate: float\n      powermean_init: float\n      residual_scale: float = 1.0\n      enable_reverse_aug: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          if (not deterministic) and self.enable_reverse_aug and (rng_key is not None):\n              mask = jax.random.bernoulli(rng_key, 0.5, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n              x = jnp.where(mask, jnp.flip(x, axis=1), x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), use_bias=True)(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvDilBlock(\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dilation=int(d),\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  residual_scale=self.residual_scale,\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = PositionDropout(self.pos_dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, C)\n\n  class Head(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic:\
    \ bool):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(h)\n\n  class DSConvPMDilAttnNet(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      d_output: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, *, deterministic: bool, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          backbone = DSConvDilBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams[\"hidden_dim\"],\n              dilations=[int(d) for d in self.hparams.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1])],\n              kernel_size=self.hparams[\"kernel_size\"],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n              pos_dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"pos_dropout_rate\"],\n              powermean_init=self.hparams[\"powermean_init\"],\n              residual_scale=self.hparams.get(\"residual_scale\", 1.0),\n              enable_reverse_aug=self.hparams.get(\"enable_reverse_aug\"\
    , False),\n          )\n          def summarize(feats):\n              # feats: (B, L, C)\n              mean_pool = jnp.mean(feats, axis=1)\n              max_pool = jnp.max(feats, axis=1)\n              pmean_pool = PowerMeanPooling(axis=1, init_p=self.hparams[\"powermean_init\"])(feats)\n              # Add attention pooling for classification tasks\n              if self.hparams.get(\"task_type\") in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n                  attn_pool = AttnPool1D(d_hidden=self.hparams.get(\"attn_hidden\", self.hparams[\"hidden_dim\"]))(\n                      feats, deterministic=deterministic\n                  )\n                  return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool, pmean_pool, attn_pool], axis=-1)\n              else:\n                  return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool, pmean_pool], axis=-1)\n\n          head = Head(\n              d_output=self.d_output,\n              hidden=self.hparams[\"head_hidden\"],\n      \
    \        dropout_rate=self.hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n          )\n\n          eval_bireverse = bool(self.hparams.get(\"eval_bireverse\", False))\n          if deterministic and eval_bireverse:\n              feats_fwd = backbone(x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n              feats_rev = backbone(jnp.flip(x, axis=1), deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n              z_fwd = summarize(feats_fwd)\n              z_rev = summarize(feats_rev)\n              logits = 0.5 * (head(z_fwd, deterministic=True) + head(z_rev, deterministic=True))\n          else:\n              feats = backbone(x, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key)\n              z = summarize(feats)\n              logits = head(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\") == \"regression\":\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class Network:\n      def __init__(self, model: nn.Module, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model\
    \ = model\n          self.hparams = hparams\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          k1, k2 = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init({'params': k1, 'dropout': k2}, dummy_input,\n                                      deterministic=True, rng_key=None)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic: bool = True, rng_key: Optional[jax.Array] = None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if (rng_key is not None and not deterministic) else None\n          return self.model.apply({'params': params}, x,\n                                  deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams[\"d_output\"]\n      model = DSConvPMDilAttnNet(hparams=hparams, d_output=d_output)\n      return Network(model, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3, weight_decay: float = 0.0095,\n                       clip: float = 0.75,\
    \ b1: float = 0.85, b2: float = 0.99):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(clip),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, b1=b1, b2=b2, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pm_v6_dil_attn.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/models')\n  from dsconv_pm_dil_attn import create_network as base_create_network\n  from dsconv_pm_dil_attn import create_optimizer as base_create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Dilated DSConv + attention pooling for classification tasks; global reverse ON\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 1e-3,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 224,\n          \"kernel_size\": 9,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"pos_dropout_rate\": 0.07,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"powermean_init\": 2.0,\n          \"residual_scale\": 0.5,\n          \"attn_hidden\"\
    : 224,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 16],\n          \"enable_reverse_aug\": True,\n          \"eval_bireverse\": True,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      h = dict(hparams)\n      # Keep reverse augmentation/eval ON globally (per v5 gains)\n      h[\"num_blocks\"] = len(h.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1]))\n      return base_create_network(h)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 1e-3):\n      # Slightly lower wd (0.0095) as it helped earlier variants\n      return base_create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0095, clip=0.75, b1=0.85, b2=0.99)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get(\"dataset\")\n      val = trial_data.get(\"val_metric\")\n      seed = trial_data.get(\"seed\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] v6-dil-attn {ds} val_metric={val} seed={seed}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv-PM v6 — Dilated DSConv + attention pooling (task-aware) + global reverse\"\ntags:\
    \ \"conv, dsconv, dilation, pooling, attention, optimizer-adamw\"\nabstract: \"Adds a lightweight attention pooling head for classification tasks atop a dilated DSConv backbone with power-mean pooling, residual scaling, and global reverse augmentation/bi-reverse eval; aims to lift ncRNA and CRI-On while retaining long-range gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pm_v6_dil_attn import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer, complete\n  from dsconv_pm_v6_dil_attn import create_network as create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating performance metrics**\n\nI need to evaluate our next steps based on the current results. Our v5 model, using dilated DSConv and dataset-aware reverse, achieved an average of 0.6445. Honestly, that’s higher than our previous score of 0.6134, but still below the state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 0.6914 from Noema II. The metrics for APA_R2 show significant improvements, sitting at 0.8375, though it’s still trailing behind the SOTA of 0.8572.**Analyzing model performance**\n\nOur current results show improvement over the previous score of 0.7853, positioning us close to the state-of-the-art (SOTA). Metrics like MRL_R2 at 0.8633, while below the SOTA of 0.8930, have improved from 0.7592. Additionally, the modified AUC-ROC is at 0.9483, quite near the SOTA of 0.9511. However, we see significant gaps in areas like ncRNA accuracy at 0.8369 versus an impressive SOTA of 0.9600, indicating a need to reassess our architecture for classification tasks.**Considering new\
  \ experiments**\n\nWe've set up v5g with global reverse across datasets (ID 938), but I’m waiting for the results. I could consider proposing additional experiments for ncRNA classification, perhaps by incorporating a small BiGRU or a 1D self-attention head, along with average pooling and a small convolution aggregator. However, I need to be mindful of keeping the architecture dataset-agnostic. The guidelines suggest that while final layers can be tailored for each prediction type, they shouldn't use dataset-specific toggles, as that might breach the rules.**Evaluating dataset-specific guidelines**\n\nI'm concerned that we might be treading close to violating the guidelines, but it’s a bit fuzzy whether that's enforced. While the system allows creating networks based on hparams['dataset'], I think we should avoid dataset-specific toggles to maintain integrity in the final paper. However, it could be useful to conduct ablation studies to observe effects. For now, v5 isn’t banned, but it’s\
  \ worth noting. I could also explore creating a unified head that improves classification without breaching dataset-agnostic principles.**Exploring model adjustments**\n\nFor CRI-On and PRS, we might need stronger regularization techniques, such as implementing dropout or label smoothing. I can't change the loss function, but I could explore temperature scaling during evaluation, even though that might not help much. Adding a stochastic position dropout for classification tasks could be beneficial, but I need to keep things simple. \n\nAdditionally, I could consider a BiGRU aggregator on top of DSConv features for classification to potentially enhance performance while adhering to the task-specific architecture rules. Lastly, the biggest gaps in performance are with ncRNA and CRI-On, so I need to focus on those areas for improvement.**Crafting v6 code**\n\nLet’s put together the v6 code. I plan to keep the dilated DSConv backbone from v5 and add an aggregator summarizer module called 'AttnPool1d'\
  \ to compute attention weights. For classification tasks, I'll combine pooling types—mean, max, pmean, and attentional pooling—while keeping regression tasks consistent with pre-existing pooling to avoid overfitting.\n\nFor implementation, I’ll customize the head by task type and possibly include a 'BiGRU aggregator,' but I'll prioritize simplicity with attention pooling. I’ll also adjust the weight decay and dropout for classification tasks, and once everything’s set, I'll finalize the submission files while ensuring proper YAML formatting."
